{
  "description": "Reading nodes typed at an earlier COMPATIBLE version of the schema's own package (kanonak-codec 0.6.1, runtime#28). deserialize resolves $type exactly, then through isReadableBy (kanonak-canonical) to the same class at a version that can read it, and keeps the written $type; typeMatches answers a generated guard the same way, subclass-aware through the optional, canonicalization-inert `ancestors` field; enumMember resolves a $ref the same way; hashing stays exact-version only. Every rejection message ends in a bracketed kind, which a port must reproduce: [unknown-type], [newer-version], [other-major], [other-minor-line], [hash-needs-exact-version]. See gen-compat-vectors/gen.ts for the full contract.",
